---
source: crates/togi/tests/cli/main.rs
expression: "help(\"night-end\")"
---
Restore the day's boot selection

Selects again exactly the boot entry `togi night` replaced, or none when the day had none or the tuning boot was picked from the boot menu. It never selects a generation of its own. It does not end the night either: the night closes when a tuning run stops or the next day's boot starts. It does not reboot: the tuning boot's shutdown hook runs it at a power-button shutdown or a reboot. Repeating it changes nothing.

Usage: togi night-end [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --state-dir <path>
          State directory
          
          [default: /var/lib/togi]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Examples:
  sudo togi night-end   Select again the boot entry the night replaced
